rem Prime Square Remainders
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=123
rem Find the least n whose remainder of
rem (p-1)^n + (p+1)^n by p^2 exceeds a
rem limit, p being the nth prime

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Limit integer = 10000000000

rem Even n leaves 2 and odd n leaves
rem 2 n p mod p^2. As p > n, n up to
rem the root of Limit suffices.
Top = Limit isqrt
Ps = primes take Top array
N = 1 to Top array
Odd' = N mod 2 equal 1
Big' = 2 * N * Ps mod (Ps * Ps)
R' = Odd choose Big 2
Hit' = R greater Limit
Answer = (N Hit) first
Answer print
